## F001 — Suspicious PowerShell Execution

```text
Finding ID: F001
Detection: DET-003
Event ID: 4104
Timestamp: 17:46:20.644
MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001 — PowerShell
```

PowerShell activity associated with the simulated attack sequence was identified during retrospective investigation.

The activity occurred immediately before the persistence stage of the attack.

### Finding

```text
Suspicious PowerShell activity was identified at 17:46:20.644.

The event occurred shortly before scheduled-task creation, establishing
a temporal relationship between execution and persistence activity.
```

---

## F002 — Scheduled Task Persistence

```text
Finding ID: F002
Detection: DET-004
Event ID: 4698
Timestamp: 17:46:39.827
MITRE ATT&CK: T1053.005 — Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task
```

The scheduled-task activity associated with the original attack simulation occurred approximately 19 seconds after the PowerShell activity identified in F001.

During retrospective investigation, Event ID 4698 could not be retrieved through the historical Splunk search.

The previously established activity timestamp was retained as part of the incident timeline, while the lack of retrievable event-level evidence was documented as an evidence gap.

### Investigation Status

```text
Activity Timestamp: 17:46:39.827
Retrospective Event Search: Unavailable
Status: Historical Evidence Gap
```

